Problem Statement
Calculate household electricity bills using progressive slabs (0-100 units @ Rs.3, 101-200 @ Rs.5, 201-300 @ Rs.7, above 300 @ Rs.9), add fixed charges (Rs.50), apply surcharge (8% if > 400 units) and rebate (5% for online payments), compare month-wise bills, and flag unusual increases exceeding 30%.

Objectives
•	Calculate tier-based energy charge accurately.
•	Incorporate fixed charges, conditional surcharges, and online rebates.
•	Compare bills across multiple billing periods to detect sudden consumption spikes (>30%).
 
Assumptions
•	Units consumed are non-negative whole numbers.
•	Slab rates apply progressively only to consumption within each respective band.
•	First month has no baseline comparison.
4. Algorithm
1. Read consumption units and payment method.
2. Compute slab charges: first 100 units at 3, next 100 at 5, next 100 at 7, remaining at 9.
3. Add fixed charge of Rs. 50.
4. If units > 400, add 8% surcharge on energy charge.
5. If online payment, subtract 5% rebate from (energy + fixed + surcharge).
6. Compare total bill with previous month; flag if increase > 30%.
